              <p>Welcome to Hana's second quarter financial review. So, our normalized profit was 278 million, which was up 169% on the quarter and 84% on the year. And that was despite a weakness in the Thai Baht of approximately 2%.</p>
              <p>Year-on-year highlights are as follows:- Sales revenues were up 3%. Normalized profit, as I mentioned earlier, was up 84% from 151 a year ago. And the margin increased 2% from 3 to 5.</p>
              <p>Our EBITDA was up nearly 50% up to 684 million and net profit was up substantially over 800%. Of course, last year was very weak. And our net cash and short-term investments were increasing 15% on the year.</p>
              <p>For the quarter, the sales revenue increased at a higher rate at 9%and normalized profits increased 170%. And you may remember in the first quarter we had a bad debt which we had to take account for. Normalized profit margin again 3%and EBITDA was up 16% to 684.</p>
              <p>So let me go through the key factors that impacted the second quarter results, starting with PMS. So we're definitely seeing a recovery in both silicon and silicon carbide. The cycle is definitely on the increase, and that helped, with reducing losses quarter-on-quarter as our sales increased, in PMS.</p>
              <p>In Ayutthaya this is our OSAT business, the IC utilization also increased, and our operating profits strengthened, over Q1 as well.</p>
              <p>In Lamphun, this is our EMS business, operating profits increased quarter-on-quarter, but it was flat year-on-year.</p>
              <p>In China, our operating profits for IC were up year-on-year, but down on the quarter, and I will go into more details. We have a large customer involved in the EV module business, and that demand is fluctuating. The EMS business in China dropped both year-on-year and quarter-on-quarter, and this is really, due to the tariff issue that the US imposed on China, most, pretty much all of our US customers left us. Fortunately, they went to our other operations in Cambodia and in Thailand. But the China operation is struggling now because we had a big drop in, in revenue, but we have reduced our cost base and that operation still remains profitable.</p>
              <p>In the USA, our RFID business was still loss-making, but we saw a significant improvement in the top line and we're working towards recovery in the second half of this year.</p>
              <p>In Cambodia, they benefited from the move out of China, so we saw increasing revenues and profit, profitability was maintained. And we measure our foreign exchange impact based on the quarter versus the past two quarters. So on that basis, there was a gain of 104 million in the second quarter. And as I mentioned earlier, cash reserves were up 50% on the year, but down 5% the quarter, but still a very healthy 11.2 billion.</p>
              <p class="th" lang="th"><span class="thtag">TH</span>ปัจจัยสำคัญที่ส่งผลต่อการกระทบการดำเนินผลประกอบการของ Q2 PMS ฟื้นตัวของความต้องการมีแรงส่งมากขึ้นแล้วก็ส่งผลให้ผลขาดทุนลดลงเมื่อเทียบกับไตรมาสก่อน</p>
              <p class="th" lang="th">ส่วน Hana อยุธยา IC อัตราการใช้กำลังผลิตเพิ่มขึ้นและก็ความสามารถในการดำเนิน การทำกำไร จากการดำเนินงานแข็งแกร่งขึ้น เทียบกับไตรมาสก่อน</p>
              <p class="th" lang="th">ส่วนฮานา ลำพูน EMS กำไรจากการดำเนินงานฟื้นตัวจากไตรมาสที่แล้วหลังจากที่ ไตรมาส 1 ได้รับผลกระทบจากหนี้สูญ แต่ก็ทรงตัวเมื่อเทียบกับปีก่อน</p>
